type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i140","start":987,"end":988},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b4-0-p1-i142","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i142","start":989,"end":1029},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b4-0-p1-i144","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i144","start":1031,"end":1063}],"metadata":{"folio":{"kind":"paragraph","frame":{"x":89.01,"y":246.57,"width":184.27,"height":299.99},"fontSize":9.96,"lineCount":25,"leading":11.95,"family":"serif","align":"left"}}},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"We introduce a new language representation model called BERT, which stands for Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers. Unlike recent language representation models (Peters et al., 2018a; Radford et al., 2018), BERT is designed to pretrain deep bidirectional representations from unlabeled text by jointly conditioning on both left and right context in all layers. As a result, the pre-trained BERT model can be finetuned with just one additional output layer to create state-of-the-art models for a wide range of tasks, such as question answering and language inference, without substantial taskspecific architecture modifications. BERT is conceptually simple and empirically powerful. It obtains new state-of-the-art results on eleven natural language processing tasks, including pushing the GLUE score to 80.5% (7.7% point absolute improvement), MultiNLI accuracy to 86.7% (4.6% absolute improvement), SQuAD v1.1 question answering Test F1 to 93.2 (1.5 point absolute improvement) and SQuAD v2.0 Test F1 to 83.1 (5.1 point absolute improvement)."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b5-0","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b5-0-p1-i146","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i146","start":0,"end":0},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b5-0-bold-p1-i146","type":"style/bold","start":0,"end":0},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b5-0-p1-i147","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i147","start":2,"end":13},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b5-0-bold-p1-i147","type":"style/bold","start":2,"end":13}],"metadata":{"folio":{"kind":"heading","frame":{"x":72,"y":558.02,"width":82.81,"height":10.76},"fontSize":11.96,"lineCount":1,"leading":13.51,"family":"serif","align":"left"}}},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 Introduction"}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i150","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i150","start":0,"end":44},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i152","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i152","start":46,"end":93},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i154","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i154","start":95,"end":144},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i156","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i156","start":146,"end":191},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i158","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i158","start":193,"end":241},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i160","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i160","start":243,"end":290},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i166","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i166","start":292,"end":302},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i167","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i167","start":304,"end":307},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i168","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i168","start":309,"end":313},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i169","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i169","start":315,"end":330},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i170","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i170","start":332,"end":337},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i175","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i175","start":339,"end":386},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i177","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i177","start":387,"end":433},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i182","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i182","start":435,"end":447},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i183","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i183","start":449,"end":450},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i184","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i184","start":452,"end":484},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i186","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i186","start":486,"end":533},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i194","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i194","start":535,"end":583},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i196","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i196","start":585,"end":593},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i197","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i197","start":595,"end":597},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i198","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i198","start":599,"end":603},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i199","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i199","start":605,"end":609},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i200","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i200","start":611,"end":629},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b6-0-p1-i202","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i202","start":631,"end":672}],"metadata":{"folio":{"kind":"paragraph","frame":{"x":72,"y":579.37,"width":218.27,"height":185.96},"fontSize":10.91,"lineCount":14,"leading":13.55,"family":"serif","align":"left"}}},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Language model pre-training has been shown to be effective for improving many natural language processing tasks (Dai and Le, 2015; Peters et al., 2018a; Radford et al., 2018; Howard and Ruder, 2018). These include sentence-level tasks such as natural language inference (Bowman et al., 2015; Williams et al., 2018) and paraphrasing (Dolan and Brockett, 2005), which aim to predict the relationships between sentences by analyzing them holistically, as well as token-level tasks such as named entity recognition and question answering, where models are required to produce fine-grained output at the token level (Tjong Kim Sang and De Meulder, 2003; Rajpurkar et al., 2016)."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i9","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i9","start":0,"end":4},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i10","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i10","start":6,"end":8},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i11","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i11","start":10,"end":12},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i12","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i12","start":14,"end":21},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i13","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i13","start":23,"end":32},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i14","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i14","start":34,"end":36},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i15","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i15","start":38,"end":42},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i22","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i22","start":43,"end":90},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i28","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i28","start":91,"end":134},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i29","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i29","start":136,"end":138},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i33","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i33","start":140,"end":152},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i34","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i34","start":154,"end":162},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i35","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i35","start":164,"end":167},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i36","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i36","start":169,"end":170},{"id":