":462,"end":463},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i71","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i71","start":465,"end":471},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i72","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i72","start":473,"end":474},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i73","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i73","start":476,"end":478},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i81","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i81","start":480,"end":525},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i87","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i87","start":526,"end":573},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i89","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i89","start":575,"end":624},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i92","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i92","start":626,"end":673},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b13-0-p1-i94","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i94","start":675,"end":707}],"metadata":{"folio":{"kind":"paragraph","frame":{"x":307.28,"y":226.05,"width":218.28,"height":199.51},"fontSize":10.91,"lineCount":15,"leading":13.55,"family":"serif","align":"left"}}},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are two existing strategies for applying pre-trained language representations to downstream tasks: feature-based and fine-tuning. The feature-based approach, such as ELMo (Peters et al., 2018a), uses task-specific architectures that include the pre-trained representations as additional features. The fine-tuning approach, such as the Generative Pre-trained Transformer (OpenAI GPT) (Radford et al., 2018), introduces minimal task-specific parameters, and is trained on the downstream tasks by simply fine-tuning all pretrained parameters. The two approaches share the same objective function during pre-training, where they use unidirectional language models to learn general language representations."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b14-0","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b14-0-p1-i96","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i96","start":0,"end":12},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b14-0-p1-i97","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i97","start":14,"end":20},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b14-0-p1-i98","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i98","start":22,"end":31},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b14-0-p1-i99","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i99","start":33,"end":40},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b14-0-p1-i100","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i100","start":42,"end":44},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b14-0-p1-i106","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i106","start":46,"end":50},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b14-0-p1-i107","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i107","start":52,"end":57},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b14-0-p1-i108","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i108","start":59,"end":69},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b14-0-p1-i109","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i109","start":71,"end":86},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b14-0-p1-i110","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i110","start":88,"end":92}],"metadata":{"folio":{"kind":"table","frame":{"x":307.28,"y":429.81,"width":218.27,"height":23.36},"fontSize":10.91,"lineCount":2,"leading":13.55,"family":"serif","align":"left"}}},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"We argue that current techniques restrict the power of the pre-trained representations, espe-"}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b15-0","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b15-0-p1-i115","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i115","start":0,"end":5},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b15-0-p1-i116","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i116","start":7,"end":9},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p1-b15-0-p1-i117","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p1-i117","start":11,"end":13},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece