-i233","start":619,"end":655}],"metadata":{"folio":{"kind":"paragraph","frame":{"x":72,"y":579.38,"width":218.81,"height":185.96},"fontSize":10.91,"lineCount":14,"leading":13.55,"family":"serif","align":"left"}}},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Learning widely applicable representations of words has been an active area of research for decades, including non-neural (Brown et al., 1992; Ando and Zhang, 2005; Blitzer et al., 2006) and neural (Mikolov et al., 2013; Pennington et al., 2014) methods. Pre-trained word embeddings are an integral part of modern NLP systems, offering significant improvements over embeddings learned from scratch (Turian et al., 2010). To pretrain word embedding vectors, left-to-right language modeling objectives have been used (Mnih and Hinton, 2009), as well as objectives to discriminate correct from incorrect words in left and right context (Mikolov et al., 2013)."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p2-b9-0","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p2-b9-0-p2-i3","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p2-i3","start":0,"end":4},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p2-b9-0-p2-i4","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p2-i4","start":6,"end":15},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p2-b9-0-p2-i5","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p2-i5","start":17,"end":20},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p2-b9-0-p2-i6","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p2-i6","start":22,"end":25},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p2-b9-0-p2-i7","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p2-i7","start":27,"end":37},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p2-b9-0-p2-i8","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p2-i8","start":39,"end":40},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p2-b9-0-p2-i10","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p2-i10","start":42,"end":48},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p2-b9-0-p2-i11","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p2-i11","start":50,"end":63},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p2-b9-0-p2-i12","type":"spatial/sour