,"end":714}],"metadata":{"folio":{"kind":"paragraph","frame":{"x":72,"y":565.48,"width":218.29,"height":199.85},"fontSize":10.91,"lineCount":15,"leading":13.55,"family":"serif","align":"left"}}},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"We introduce BERT and its detailed implementation in this section. There are two steps in our framework: pre-training and fine-tuning. During pre-training, the model is trained on unlabeled data over different pre-training tasks. For finetuning, the BERT model is first initialized with the pre-trained parameters, and all of the parameters are fine-tuned using labeled data from the downstream tasks. Each downstream task has separate fine-tuned models, even though they are initialized with the same pre-trained parameters. The question-answering example in Figure 1 will serve as a running example for this section. A distinctive feature of BERT is its unified architecture across different tasks. There is mini-"}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p3-b8-0","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p3-b8-0-p3-i77","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p3-i77","start":0,"end":21},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p3-b8-0-p3-i78","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p3-i78","start":23,"end":25},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p3-b8-0-p3-i79","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p3-i79","start":27,"end":46},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p3-b8-0-p3-i81","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p3-i81","start":47,"end":89}],"metadata":{"folio":{"kind":"paragraph","frame":{"x":307.28,"y":341.45,"width":218.27,"height":23.36},"fontSize":10.91,"lineCount":2,"leading":13.55,"family":"serif","align":"left"}}},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"mal difference between the pre-trained architecture and the final downstream architecture."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p3-b8-1","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p3-b8-1-p3-i83","type"