e":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i165","start":696,"end":741},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b8-1-p8-i167","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i167","start":743,"end":756},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b8-1-p8-i168","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i168","start":758,"end":778},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b8-1-p8-i169","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i169","start":780,"end":785},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b8-1-p8-i171","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i171","start":787,"end":811},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b8-1-p8-i172","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i172","start":813,"end":834},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b8-1-p8-i181","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i181","start":835,"end":876},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b8-1-p8-i185","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i185","start":878,"end":923},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b8-1-p8-i187","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i187","start":925,"end":966}],"metadata":{"folio":{"kind":"paragraph","frame":{"x":72,"y":387.09,"width":218.28,"height":282.15},"fontSize":10.91,"lineCount":21,"leading":13.55,"family":"serif","align":"left"}}},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"No NSP: A bidirectional model which is trained using the \"masked LM\" (MLM) but without the \"next sentence prediction\" (NSP) task. LTR & No NSP: A left-context-only model which is trained using a standard Left-to-Right (LTR) LM, rather than an MLM. The left-only constraint was also applied at fine-tuning, because removing it introduced a pre-train/fine-tune mismatch that degraded downstream performance. Additionally, this model was pre-trained without the NSP task. This is directly comparable to OpenAI GPT, but using our larger training dataset, our input representation, and our fine-tuning scheme. We first examine the impact brought by the NSP task. In Table 5, we show that removing NSP hurts performance significantly on QNLI, MNLI, and SQuAD 1.1. Next, we evaluate the impact of training bidirectional representations by comparing \"No NSP\" to \"LTR & No NSP\". The LTR model performs worse than the MLM model on all tasks, with large drops on MRPC and SQuAD."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i192","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i192","start":0,"end":26},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i193","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i193","start":28,"end":32},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i194","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i194","start":34,"end":37},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i195","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i195","start":39,"end":43},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i201","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i201","start":45,"end":69},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i202","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i202","start":71,"end":72},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i203","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i203","start":74,"end":91},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i211","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i211","start":93,"end":141},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i220","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i220","start":142,"end":154},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i221","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i221","start":156,"end":157},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i222","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i222","start":159,"end":166},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i223","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i223","start":168,"end":187},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i232","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i232","start":188,"end":234},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i236","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i236","start":236,"end":282},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i244","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i244","start":284,"end":312},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b9-0-p8-i245","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i245","start":314,"end":330}],"metadata":{"folio":{"kind":"paragraph","frame":{"x":72,"y":674.22,"width":218.27,"height":91.11},"fontSize":10.91,"lineCount":7,"leading":13.55,"family":"serif","align":"left"}}},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"For SQuAD it is intuitively clear that a LTR model will perform poorly at token predictions, since the token-level hidden states have no rightside context. In order to make a good faith attempt at strengthening the LTR system, we added a randomly initialized BiLSTM on top. This does significantly improve results on SQuAD, but the"}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b11-0","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b11-0-p8-i66","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i66","start":0,"end":2},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b11-0-bold-p8-i66","type":"style/bold","start":0,"end":2},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b11-0-p8-i67","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i67","start":4,"end":23},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b11-0-bold-p8-i67","type":"style/bold","start":4,"end":23}],"metadata":{"folio":{"kind":"heading","frame":{"x":307.28,"y":257.81,"width":118.16,"height":9.83},"fontSize":10.91,"lineCount":1,"leading":12.33,"family":"serif","align":"left"}}},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"5.2 Effect of Model Size"}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b12-0","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b12-0-p8-i68","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i68","start":0,"end":51},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b12-0-p8-i71","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i71","start":53,"end":101},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p8-b12-0-p8-i73","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p8-i7