{"folio":{"kind":"caption","frame":{"x":72,"y":184.22,"width":453.55,"height":56.79},"fontSize":9.96,"lineCount":5,"leading":11.96,"family":"serif","align":"left"}}},"inline":[{"kind":"text","text":"Figure 3: Differences in pre-training model architectures. BERT uses a bidirectional Transformer. OpenAI GPT uses a left-to-right Transformer. ELMo uses the concatenation of independently trained left-to-right and right-toleft LSTMs to generate features for downstream tasks. Among the three, only BERT representations are jointly conditioned on both left and right context in all layers. In addition to the architecture differences, BERT and OpenAI GPT are fine-tuning approaches, while ELMo is a feature-based approach."}]},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p13-b8-0","type":"standoff-editor-block","properties":{"standoffProperties":[{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p13-b8-0-p13-i72","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p13-i72","start":0,"end":1},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p13-b8-0-p13-i73","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p13-i73","start":3,"end":11},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p13-b8-0-p13-i74","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p13-i74","start":13,"end":46},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p13-b8-0-p13-i83","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p13-i83","start":48,"end":94},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p13-b8-0-p13-i85","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p13-i85","start":95,"end":138},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p13-b8-0-p13-i86","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p13-i86","start":140,"end":142},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p13-b8-0-p13-i89","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p13-i89","start":144,"end":146},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p13-b8-0-p13-i90","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p13-i90","start":148,"end":186},{"id":"folio-987545ffb087f1ece898-p13-b8-0-p13-i92","type":"spatial/source-run","value":"p13-i92","start":188,"end":228}],"metadata":{"folio":{"kind":"paragraph","frame":{"x":72,"y":265.86,"width":218.28,"hei